# Capture verification

Use temporary capture roots and freeze wall/monotonic clocks where timing is
asserted. Stop/deadlock probes must have bounded waits and safe cleanup.
Exercise recording HTTP conflicts and server-owned client state, including
failed/stale reads and the real Gateway warning path. Replay UI tests must click
Load, candle/trade downloads, Pause/Resume and check POST bodies and visible errors.
Verify timers stop after unmount. Tape assertions must preserve recorded prices
and avoid inventing bid/ask or trade direction.

Use Vitest's default or dot reporter, never the removed basic reporter. Check
reported nonzero test counts as well as exit status. Existing parked UX/fidelity
issues keep their own scope; coverage is not evidence that those issues shipped.

Fresh worktrees install frontend dependencies with npm ci. A shared node_modules
link is not evidence that the locked dependency tree is complete. Native option
disablement is verified through its disabled DOM property in browser tests.
